  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Saying «in case»: lỡ… thì…, phòng khi",
     "texto": [
      "**Lỡ (ra)** + something bad + **thì**… = what if (unfortunately) … happens…, in case…: «**Lỡ** một trong hai đứa mất việc **thì** sao?» = What if one of the two of you loses their job? It talks about a risk you don't want, but that might come. In the north **nhỡ** is also used.",
      "**Phòng khi** + what might happen = just in case, as a precaution: «Mình nên có một khoản **phòng khi** ốm đau» = We should have some money just in case one of us falls ill.",
      "**Để dành** = to keep for later: «**để dành** tiền». **Dự phòng** = reserve: «quỹ **dự phòng**» = emergency fund.",
      "The difference with «nếu»: «nếu» is neutral. «Lỡ» always looks at something **bad**; that's why it's the word of someone who plans ahead… or of someone who worries too much."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
